$CATEGORY: Q10 - Conditionals and logic

::Q10_01:: boolean - A data type with only two possible values, true and false. {TRUE}

::Q10_02:: relational operator - compares two values and produces a boolean indicating the relationship between them.{TRUE}

::Q10_03:: conditional statement - A statement that uses a condition to determine which statements to execute.{TRUE}

::Q10_04:: block - sequence of statements, surrounded by curly braquets, that generally runs as the result of a condition.{TRUE}

::Q10_05:: branch - one of the alternative blocks after a conditional statement.{TRUE}

::Q10_06:: chaining - {
    =A way of joining several conditional statements in sequence.
    ~Putting a conditional statement inside one or both branches of another conditional statement.
}

::Q10_07a:: given the statement on the whiteboard (for) identify its type {
    =nesting
    ~chaining
}

::Q10_07b:: given the statement on the whiteboard (if) identify its type {
    ~nesting
    =chaining
}

::Q10_08:: logical operator - combines boolean values and produces a boolean value. 
The \=\= operator is one of them {FALSE#Nop! it's a relational operator}

::Q10_09:: flag - variable (usually boolean) that represents a condition or status.{TRUE}

::Q10_10:: validate - to confirm that an input value is of the correct type and within the expected range.{TRUE}
